% --- S13. Nil gain, $1 gain, deducted amounts, and the cost base / reduced
% cost base gap ----------------------------------------------------------------
% Working [statute]: d1 proceeds 1000 = cost base 1000: neither gain nor loss
% (s 104-10(4) needs "more than" or "less than"). d2 proceeds 1001: gain 1.
% d3: acquired 2024, cost 120, deducted 30: s 110-45(2) removes the 30 from the
% cost base (90) and s 110-55(4) from the reduced cost base (90); proceeds 100
% > 90: gain 10. d4: acquired 1990 (before 13 May 1997): s 110-45(2) does not
% apply, cost base 120, reduced cost base 90; proceeds 100 are not more than
% 120 and not less than 90: neither a gain nor a loss. Net capital gain
% 1 + 10 = 11 (both held 6 months: no discount).
scenario s13 nil and one dollar is:
    lambda is an entity of kind individual.
    d1 is a disposal of shares six by lambda.
    d1 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    shares six was acquired by lambda on 2024-09-01.
    d1 has money proceeds of 1000.
    shares six has first element cost of 1000.
    d2 is a disposal of shares seven by lambda.
    d2 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    shares seven was acquired by lambda on 2024-09-01.
    d2 has money proceeds of 1001.
    shares seven has first element cost of 1000.
    d3 is a disposal of building one by lambda.
    d3 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    building one was acquired by lambda on 2024-09-01.
    d3 has money proceeds of 100.
    building one has first element cost of 120.
    building one has deducted amounts of 30.
    d4 is a disposal of building two by lambda.
    d4 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    building two was acquired by lambda on 1990-09-01.
    d4 has money proceeds of 100.
    building two has first element cost of 120.
    building two has deducted amounts of 30.
    cost base expects answers ["the cost base of shares six is 1000", "the cost base of shares seven is 1000", "the cost base of building one is 90", "the cost base of building two is 120"].
    reduced cost base expects answers ["the reduced cost base of shares six is 1000", "the reduced cost base of shares seven is 1000", "the reduced cost base of building one is 90", "the reduced cost base of building two is 90"].
    gain expects answers ["d2 gives a capital gain of 1", "d3 gives a capital gain of 10"].
    loss expects answers [].
    disregarded expects answers [].
    net gain expects answers ["the net capital gain of lambda for the income year 2025 is 11.00"].

% --- S14. Section 118-20: amount otherwise assessable ------------------------
% Working [statute]: d1 gain 30000 does not exceed the 40000 included under
% s 6-5: reduced to zero (s 118-20(2), the Act's example); d2 gain 50000
% exceeds the 20000 included: reduced to 30000 (s 118-20(3)); both held under
% 12 months: no discount; net capital gain 30000.
scenario s14 otherwise assessable is:
    mu is an entity of kind individual.
    d1 is a disposal of lot one by mu.
    d1 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    lot one was acquired by mu on 2024-09-01.
    d1 has money proceeds of 130000.
    lot one has first element cost of 100000.
    40000 of the gain from d1 is included in assessable income under another provision.
    d2 is a disposal of lot two by mu.
    d2 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    lot two was acquired by mu on 2024-09-01.
    d2 has money proceeds of 150000.
    lot two has first element cost of 100000.
    20000 of the gain from d2 is included in assessable income under another provision.
    disregarded expects answers ["the capital gain or loss from d1 is disregarded because subsection 118-20(2) gain reduced to zero by the amount otherwise assessable"].
    gain expects answers ["d2 gives a capital gain of 30000"].
    net gain expects answers ["the net capital gain of mu for the income year 2025 is 30000.00"].

% --- S15. Market value substitution on both sides -----------------------------
% Working [statute]: house acquired from a parent for no consideration: first
% element = market value 300000 at acquisition (s 112-20(1)(a)); sold to a
% sibling not at arm's length: proceeds = market value 450000 at the event
% (s 116-30(2)(b)(i)), not the 100000 paid; gain 150000; held since 2015:
% discount; net capital gain 75000.
scenario s15 market value substitution is:
    nu is an entity of kind individual.
    d1 is a disposal of house one by nu.
    d1 has contract date 2025-03-01.
    house one was acquired by nu on 2015-06-01.
    house one was acquired for no consideration.
    house one had a market value of 300000 when acquired.
    d1 was not at arm s length.
    d1 has money proceeds of 100000.
    house one had a market value of 450000 at the time of d1.
    proceeds expects answers ["the capital proceeds from d1 are 450000"].
    cost base expects answers ["the cost base of house one is 300000"].
    gain expects answers ["d1 gives a capital gain of 150000"].
    net gain expects answers ["the net capital gain of nu for the income year 2025 is 75000.00"].

